large** errors — regime boundaries, releases, the","+   wrong time of day — not from polishing a global scale."," ","-## 2. Approach","+**The right benchmark.** The per-prompt 10th percentile of the field is not reachable by any","+single miner (it mixes different miners on different prompts): over 2026-08-05..08-26 the best","+single miner was +2.1% (1h), +1.1% (crypto-24h), +1.2% (com-equ) above it, and the top of the","+field is a block of clones with identical scores. I therefore report CRPS against the **best","+single miner** (chosen ex post, with full coverage) next to the starter."," ","-A closed-form, CPU-only model (≈50 ms per 24h prompt, ≈25 ms per 1h prompt, no weights):","+## 2. Approach — the champion (v7)"," ","-1. **Weekly volatility profile keyed on New York time** (minute of the week, 10,080 buckets, per","-   asset), fitted offline on the snapshot. Keying on New York (not UTC) keeps the US open, the","-   08:30 releases and the 16:00 close in place across daylight-saving switches. The profile is a","-   *robust* shape (mean absolute return per bucket, squared), smoothed ±4 min, with the","-   minute-of-hour pattern restored (the first minute of each hour/half-hour is 20-25% more active),","-   and fitted with scheduled-event windows excluded.","-2. **Level**: three EWMAs (fast / medium / slow) of the deseasonalised absolute returns found in","-   the context, mixed with weights that depend on the lead time (HAR-style term structure).","-3. **Scheduled events** from the calendar the miner receives (CPI, NFP, PPI, retail sales,","-   GDP/PCE, FOMC, earnings): a variance multiplier for each window after the release, fitted as","-   the median effect of past releases of the same type.","-4. **Paths**: Student-t(5) innovations × a per-path log-normal variance multiplier (the level is","-   uncertain), plus exactly-zero steps at the profiled share (stale minutes are real).","+A closed-form, CPU-only model. No weights; two small artifacts fitted offline on the snapshot","+(`profiles.npz`, `events.json`). ~0.1 s per 24h prompt and ~0.03 s per 1h prompt."," ","-*(Sections 3-6 are completed at the end of the campaign.)*","+1. **Weekly volatility profile keyed on New York time** — per asset, one value per minute of the","+   week (10,080 buckets), separately for 1-min and 5-min returns. New-York keying keeps the US","+   open, the 08:30 releases and the 16:00 close in place across DST switches (the hourly profile","+   of every asset, crypto included, is more peaked on the NY clock than on UTC). The shape is","+   *robust*: mean absolute return per bucket (squared), normalised by a centred 7-day level so","+   calm and wild weeks weigh the same, smoothed ±4 min, the minute-of-hour pattern restored after","+   smoothing (the first minute of each hour is 20-50% more active), and fitted **with scheduled","+   event windows excluded**.","+2. **Level**: three EWMAs (fast / medium / slow) of the deseasonalised absolute k-minute returns","+   in the context (k = the prompt's step). The forecast level at each lead is a convex mix of","+   them whose weights depend on the lead (HAR-like term structure, weights fitted by QLIKE):","+   24h crypto: half-lives 1h/6h/8d, weights (.45,.40,.15) at lead 0-1h → (0,.70,.30) at 12-24h;","+   equities: (.65,.25,.10) → (.05,.45,.50); 1h: half-lives 10m/1h/8h, (.55,.20,.25) → (.20,.25,.55).","+3. **Scheduled events** from the calendar the miner receives (`$SYNTH_BENCHMARK_CALENDAR`):","+   variance multipliers per window after the release (median effect of past releases of the","+   type, by asset group). E.g. CPI: ×101 (crypto) / ×58 (equities) in the first minute, ×9 / ×6","+   for minutes 1-5, ×3.9 / ×2.0 for 5-15; FOMC ×7 / ×4.6 at 30-60 min (press conference);","+   earnings ×60-130 for the first two hours after the release, ×3.3 overnight. Context returns","+   inside event windows are deflated by the same multipliers before entering the level EWMAs.","+4. **Paths**: per-step variance = scale × level(lead) × profile(minute of week) × event","+   multiplier. Innovations are Student-t, multiplied by a per-path log-normal variance factor","+   (level uncertainty): t(5) and sd 0.35 for 24h; t(7) and sd 0.6 for 1h. Exactly-zero steps at","+   the profiled share of stale minutes; prices rounded to the venue's price grid when it is","+   coarse (SOL, XRP: ~1 bp ticks). **Stratified (Latin-hypercube) draws**: every step's draws and","+   the per-path factors cover all 1000 strata.","+","+## 3. Experiments (failures included)","+","+Validation: walk-forward windows (A: profiles/events fitted before 2026-08-01, scored","+08-05..08-26; B: fitted before 10-01, scored 10-08..10-29; C: 10-29..11-08, after the NY DST","+switch; S: a holdout never used for any decision). Paired comparisons on identical prompts;","+a change is kept only if it helps on both A and B in most asset cells.","+","+| # | change | result (CRPS change; negative = better) | verdict |","+|---|---|---|---|","+| 1 | v1: NY-time weekly profile × EWMA, t + mixture, vs starter | -3..-16% in all 18 asset cells | keep |","+| 2 | v2: HAR 3-EWMA lead-dependent level (QLIKE-fitted) | A: crypto-24h -0.6%, com-equ -6.7%, 1h -2.0% (all cells) | keep |","+| 3 | exactly-zero steps (staleness) | 0.00 .. -0.15% | keep (cheap) |","+| 4 | weekend-only level for weekend steps | +0.01..+0.10% | discard |","+| 5 | **robust (mean-|r|) level and profile** | com-equ A -0.71%, B -0.45%; crypto -0.04/-0.22% | keep |","+| 6 | fast intra-path stochastic volatility | +0.05..+0.5% (all cells worse) | discard |","+| 7 | CONTEXT_DAYS 10/14/30 vs 21 | within ±0.05% | keep 21 |","+| 8 | lead-growing level uncertainty (log-variance random walk) | sign flips A→B | discard |","+| 9 | **calendar events** (walk-forward multipliers) | CPI-spanning 1h prompts -5.7% (A) / -10.4% (B); earnings-spanning com-equ prompts -3.9 / -7.8 / -9.9% (A/B/C); all prompts -0.02..-0.49% | keep (EIA dropped: mixed) |","+| 10 | minute-of-hour pattern in the profile | -0.01..-0.04%, every cell same sign | keep |","+| 11 | knobs (scale, mixing sd, t dof) around the optimum | ±0.16%, com-equ winners on A flip on B | no change |","+| 12 | high-low range in the level measure | ±0.04%, signs flip | discard |","+| 13 | **price-grid rounding** (SOL, XRP) | 1h: SOL -0.21/-0.11%, XRP -0.11/-0.06% (A/B) | keep |","+| 14 | profile exponent 0.9/1.1; weekend variance ×0.8/×1.25 | flips / worse | no change |","+| 15 | slow-heavy weights for weekend steps (Friday-afternoon problem) | crypto +0.3..+1.4% in A, -0.1% in C | discard |","+| 16 | mixing sd growing with fast/slow disagreement | ~0 | discard |","+| 17 | **stratified draws** (removes the N=1000 ensemble bias, ≈ E|X-X'|/2N) | -0.06..-0.08% in every cell of A, B and C | keep |","+| 18 | other EWMA half-lives | the fitted ones are optimal on both windows | no change |","+| 19 | trade count as a vol predictor | +0.000..+0.003 R² over the HAR forecast | discard |","+| 20 | 1h: wider per-path dispersion, thinner step tails (realised-vol PIT was U-shaped) | A -0.04%, B -0.05% | keep |","+","+Explained anomalies worth sharing:","+","+* **Weekends of the Hyperliquid equity/commodity perps are a separate regime.** Saturday 5-min","+  returns are exactly zero 42% of the time for XAU (10-17% for tokenised stocks) and weekend","+  activity varies 10× between weekends. A mean-square profile overstated the typical weekend by","+  ~2.5× for XAU; the robust profile fixed most of the Saturday gap (+8.5% → +1-2.5% vs field p10).","+* **Hot Friday sessions followed by dead weekends** remain our worst com-equ prompts (SP500,","+  AAPLX starting Friday 16:00-23:00 NY: +30-40% vs the field median). Every fix I tried helped in","+  late October and hurt in August — whether the weekend follows Friday is itself regime-dependent.","+* **The best 1h miner wins when the hour turns out calmer than forecast**, and the PIT of the","+  realised hourly volatility inside our paths was U-shaped: our paths' realised volatility was","+  too concentrated (fixed partly by #20).","+","+## 4. Results","+","+**Official backtester** (`agent/predict.py`, 1000 paths, validator prompt times, the 10 days of","+scored prompts before 2026-11-08; in-sample for the champion's artifacts), mean CRPS over assets:","+","+| configuration | starter | champion v7 | change |","+|---|---|---|---|","+| CRYPTO_24H (5 assets, 1200 prompts) | 4606.76 | 4436.95 | -3.69% |","+| COM_EQU_24H (8 assets, 870 prompts) | 3304.04 | 3037.12 | -8.08% |","+| CRYPTO_1H (5 assets, 7200 prompts) | 988.40 | 925.40 | -6.37% |","+","+**Out of sample** (walk-forward artifacts), CRPS relative to the best single field miner:","+","+| window | CRYPTO_24H | COM_EQU_24H | CRYPTO_1H |","+|---|---|---|---|","+| A (08-05..08-26; 1h to 08-15, field without vol term) | +0.1% (v3) | -0.2% (v3) | +0.6% (v3, biased) |","+| C (10-29..11-08) | +0.24% (v6) | +0.54% (v6) | +0.39% (v6) |","+| **S holdout (09-05..09-26; 1h 09-23..10-03), v7** | **-0.01%** | **+0.00%** | **-0.16%** |","+","+On the untouched holdout the champion matches the best single miner of the field in all three","+configurations, and beats the starter by 3.2% / 12.7% / 4.4%.","+","+## 5. Limitations","+","+* The 24h comparisons rest on ~20-day windows; asset-level differences below ~0.1% are noise","+  (they flip sign between windows), so the model is tuned at the group level only.","+* Event multipliers are medians over ~10-15 releases per type (pooled over assets); they are","+  fitted leave-window-out, but types with few occurrences (FOMC, earnings) stay noisy. The","+  evaluation window holds CPI (11-10), PPI (11-13), retail sales (11-17) and NVDA earnings","+  (11-18, 21:00 UTC); a release moved after the cutoff is not in the calendar.","+* NYSE holidays are not modelled (none in the evaluation window; Thanksgiving is 11-26).","+* The Friday-session → weekend transition and the August-type regimes are not solved.","+* No cross-asset information (simulate() sees one asset's context) and no sub-minute data.","+","+## 6. With more budget","+","+1. A regime-switching weekend model for the tokenised equities (the remaining worst prompts).","+2. Holiday profiles (NYSE_CLOSED / early close) for live robustness.","+3. Per-asset event multipliers once more releases accumulate, and an explicit model of the","+   earnings-day open (the overnight multiplier is coarse).","+4. A learned (GPU) correction of the level forecast on top of the HAR terms — the QLIKE R² of","+   0.66-0.78 for the next hour leaves room, but trade counts and ranges added nothing, so the","+   inputs would have to be new (other assets' contexts are not available to simulate())."]}],"originalFile":"# A seasonal, event-aware volatility model for Synth SN50 — campaign-7 report\n\n*Audience: Synth miners. Everything here was measured with synth-lib's own scorer\n(`score_crps` / `backtest`), on the validator's real prompt times, over the frozen snapshot\n(2025-08-01 → 2026-11-08). Lower CRPS is better.*\n\n## 1. Context\n\nA Synth miner answers a prompt `(asset, start_time, horizon)` with 1000 simulated price paths. The\nvalidator scores the fan with CRPS on many interval returns at once:\n\n| configuration | what is summed (each a CRPS in basis points) | share of our CRPS |\n|---|---|---|\n| CRYPTO_24H / COM_EQU_24H (5-min steps, 289 points) | 288 5-min returns, 48 30-min returns, 8 3-h returns, the final price | 61% / 25% / 11% / 4% |\n| CRYPTO_1H (1-min steps, 61 points) | 60 1-min, 30 2-min, 12 5-min, 4 15-min, 2 30-min returns, final price, 12 \"gap\" returns from the start (5..60 min), plus a volatility term | 26 / 19 / 12 / 7 / 5 / 3.5 / 28 / 1 % |\n\nTwo consequences drive everything below:\n\n1. In the 24h configurations, **60% of the score is the 288 individual 5-minute returns**. What\n   matters most is the per-step volatility *profile* over the day, not the 24-hour total.\n2. In the 1h configuration, the very short returns and the cumulative \"gap\" returns dominate,\n   so the **current** volatility (the last tens of minutes) is what counts.\n\n## 2. Approach\n\nA closed-form, CPU-only model (≈50 ms per 24h prompt, ≈25 ms per 1h prompt, no weights):\n\n1. **Weekly volatility profile keyed on New York time** (minute of the week, 10,080 buckets, per\n   asset), fitted offline on the snapshot. Keying on New York (not UTC) keeps the US open, the\n   08:30 releases and the 16:00 close in place across daylight-saving switches. The profile is a\n   *robust* shape (mean absolute return per bucket, squared), smoothed ±4 min, with the\n   minute-of-hour pattern restored (the first minute of each hour/half-hour is 20-25% more active),\n   and fitted with scheduled-event windows excluded.\n2. **Level**: three EWMAs (fast / medium / slow) of the deseasonalised absolute returns found in\n   the context, mixed with weights that depend on the lead time (HAR-style term structure).\n3. **Scheduled events** from the calendar the miner receives (CPI, NFP, PPI, retail sales,\n   GDP/PCE, FOMC, earnings): a variance multiplier for each window after the release, fitted as\n   the median effect of past releases of the same type.\n4. **Paths**: Student-t(5) innovations × a per-path log-normal variance multiplier (the level is\n   uncertain), plus exactly-zero steps at the profiled share (stale minutes are real).\n\n*(Sections 3-6 are completed at the end of the campaign.)*\n","userModified":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01Ai93x3V1gRWAqeLLpKpbn1","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
